Make the application responsive without sacrificing correctness.

Investigate:

- Model loading time.
- Per-request inference time.
- Image size and encoding overhead.
- Unnecessary repeated model initialization.
- Redundant API calls.
- Frame-processing frequency.
- Memory consumption.
- Backend concurrency.
- Request cancellation.
- Provider rate limits.
- Deployment cold starts.
- Frontend bundle size where relevant.

Choose optimizations that fit the actual hosting environment. If the deployment has insufficient memory for the selected model, select a feasible architecture or hosting option rather than leaving the feature permanently unavailable.

Report local and deployed performance separately.

Do not claim a performance improvement without measuring it under comparable conditions.

